WEBVTT

00:00:00.143 --> 00:00:03.897
One important preprocessing idea is data leakage.

00:00:03.897 --> 00:00:08.807
If we fit a scaler or learned encoder using the entire dataset before evaluation,

00:00:08.807 --> 00:00:13.067
information from validation or test data can influence the transformation.

00:00:13.067 --> 00:00:20.212
A safer workflow fits learned preprocessing on the training data and applies the fitted transformation to

00:00:20.212 --> 00:00:20.537
validation or test data.

00:00:20.537 --> 00:00:27.042
Module 1 is not a machine-learning module, but this habit is worth establishing now because preprocessing can

00:00:27.042 --> 00:00:29.197
affect the honesty of later evaluation.

00:00:29.197 --> 00:00:34.232
Preprocessing is not neutral: it tells software how to interpret the variable.

00:00:34.232 --> 00:00:40.897
One-hot encoding avoids inventing rank for nominal categories; ordinal coding preserves a known order;

00:00:40.897 --> 00:00:45.017
scaling changes numerical representation but not conceptual meaning.

00:00:45.017 --> 00:00:51.280
In predictive work, learned preprocessing should be fitted only on training data so evaluation remains honest.
